# Line endings for the launchers and installers, stated rather than left to
# whatever core.autocrlf happens to be on the machine that commits.
#
# A .command or .sh file with CRLF endings fails on macOS with
#   bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M
# and a .bat file is the opposite case: cmd.exe can mis-handle goto and labels
# in a file that has only LF.
#
# The catch-all comes first on purpose: within a .gitattributes the last
# matching pattern wins, so the specific rules must follow it, not precede it.
*          text=auto

*.command  text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.bat      text eol=crlf
